From 094e3e203c56e7753ddba505f9bfb2e67421a62a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joethedev5 <deepsbx1@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:50:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Recover the hypervisor context conversion path

convert_context_by_guest selects the source and destination buffers,
sizes and measurements from the direction, then branches on the guest's
major-version and context-measurement mismatches.  With both mismatches
the context goes through kif_intermediate: native to intermediate (the
supported layout of the shared version) and then intermediate to
shared, or the reverse for shared to native.  A major-version-only
mismatch goes through the major-version conversion helper, a
measurement-only mismatch converts directly, and a shared-to-native
conversion after a major mismatch stamps the kernel interface frame's
read-only root with the ARM hypervisor state version.

hv_convert_context_major_version is the unimplemented major-version
conversion: its body is assert(false), so development and kasan kernels
panic at the three call sites while release kernels, where assert() is
empty, fall through to the explicit kif_intermediate conversions.  The
helper's descriptor, the assertion texts and the release build's three
conversion sites all match the reference.

Also give the read-only context root its recovered members (ver, exit,
controls, state, ich, sme_state, misc), define ARM_HV_STATE_VER, declare
the file's external inline helpers, and drop a spurious assert from
hv_get_state_version_major, matching the reference header.

Authored-By: joethedev5 <joeshmo@nunya.com>
